schema: "0.4"
id: npl-prism-47-market-competitor-research
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo creative suite — Market & Competitor Research: track competitors
# within a market segment and research/track keywords to inform campaign strategy.
# Theme tenets: luminous frosted glass, cool violet→cyan spectrum gradient, Sora
# geometric type, 16px radius; research data tables stay on a solid surface.
# Palette: violet #7c3aed, cyan #06b6d4, fuchsia #d946ef, canvas #f7f8ff, ink #1a1730.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    PREMIUM market-research workspace inside a modern AI product. Polished, analytical,
    composed. Frosted-glass framing panels float over a pale spectrum mesh, but the
    dense research tables sit on solid, legible surfaces. The signature violet→cyan
    gradient appears only on the primary action and glass edges. Clean geometric
    sans-serif (Sora), no serif.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the MARKET & COMPETITOR RESEARCH screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo's creative suite.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three bands): a slim LEFT app nav rail (achromatic glass), a
    dominant CENTER research area split into two stacked sections, and a RIGHT ~320px
    KEYWORD panel — over a pale near-white canvas (#f7f8ff) with a soft blurred
    violet/cyan spectrum mesh glowing through the glass framing.

    HEADER BAND: "Market Research" title in Sora 700, and a MARKET SEGMENT SELECTOR — a
    prominent glass dropdown pill showing the active segment (e.g. "SaaS / DevTools")
    with a small chevron; a "Track competitor" primary button (violet→cyan gradient,
    soft glow) at the right.

    CENTER TOP — COMPETITOR TRACKING TABLE: a card whose glass FRAME is frosted but whose
    TABLE BODY is a solid opaque white surface for legibility. Columns: Competitor /
    Segment / Traffic / Last seen. A few rows of real-looking competitor names with small
    favicons, a traffic trend sparkline per row (thin cyan line), and a quiet status dot.
    Header row carries a thin gradient underline accent only.

    CENTER LOWER / RIGHT — KEYWORD RESEARCH PANEL: a glass panel with a search field
    (glass, opaque inner backing) and a results list of keyword rows — each showing the
    keyword, a volume number, a difficulty meter (small horizontal bar), and a "＋ track"
    glass button. One row is already tracked (flat violet "tracked" chip).

    RIGHT LOWER — TRACKED KEYWORD LIST: a compact glass panel titled "Tracked" listing
    saved keywords as pill chips with a small remove ✕, each pill a soft spectrum-tinted
    translucent fill.

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool near-white canvas + soft spectrum mesh; ink #1a1730 text; the
    violet(#7c3aed)→cyan(#06b6d4) gradient only on the primary "Track competitor" button,
    glass edges, and the single cyan sparkline/meter accent; status chips flat opaque.
    Sora everywhere, no serif; small numeric data may use JetBrains Mono for alignment.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: 16px radius on cards/panels, pill chips, translucent frosted glass
    with backdrop blur and gradient-sheen edges for framing — but the competitor table
    body is a solid opaque surface. Violet-tinted soft shadows; luminous, premium.

    MOOD: premium, analytical, organized. A research cockpit that presents in glass and
    color but tabulates in solid, legible rows.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, gradient body text, gradient status chips, rainbow tie-dye buttons, a data table rendered as unreadable translucent glass, neon-on-black cyberpunk"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches key components — Competitor Tracking Table, Market Segment Selector, Keyword Research Panel, Tracked Keyword List"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Prism frosted-glass framing over a spectrum mesh, violet→cyan gradient on primary action/edges/single accent only, Sora type, 16px radius; the research table body correctly on a solid surface"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear split between competitor table and keyword research, plausible real-product analytical layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, legible table/numeric text, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "the research data table rendered as low-legibility translucent glass"
    - "gradient status chips, gradient body text, or rainbow chrome"

tags: [npl-prism, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup, creative-suite]
